{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-3100"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of furniture"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "3100"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :furniture-manufacturing/plant-operations
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :consumer-safety :resource-efficiency]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :furniture-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "FurnitureAdvisor ⊣ Furniture Plant Operations Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS COORDINATION
 actor for furniture manufacturing (cutting, joinery/assembly, sanding,
 finishing/upholstery lines) -- not direct cutting/joinery/finishing-
 line-equipment operation authority. Four ops (`:log-production-batch`
 / `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-safety-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Ten concrete
 governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD invariants:
 propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect
 allowlist (no direct cutting/joinery/finishing-line-equipment
 control), permanent line-control-finalize block, independent
 equipment verification/registration before maintenance scheduling,
 independent batch verification/registration before shipment
 coordination, independent shipment-unit recompute against the batch's
 own logged unit-count, double-schedule guard, quality-grade
 validation, and defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern
 flagging (materials-safety / VOC finish-fume exposure, equipment
 safety, labor safety) ALWAYS escalates to a human plant supervisor;
 `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and
 only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
